  "faithful": "In the following experiments an effay cwt. was always employed, unless where it is expressly mentioned otherwise; conclusions sufficiently accurate may indeed be obtained from 25 lb. may sometimes from smaller quantities. In these cases our author mentions the usual quantity; applying to them those formulae of calculation which are founded on the mutual proportions of the proximate principles constituting metallic faults. By an easy fublition, the same formulae may be used by those who employ ½ or ¼ cwt. We now come to describe the method of effaying the ores of the particular metals.",
